WEBVTT

00:00.240 --> 00:01.590
Instructor: Welcome to the next section.

00:01.590 --> 00:04.230
Hopefully you survived the Intro to Git Hub,

00:04.230 --> 00:06.780
as well as the new commands, like Git Clone,

00:06.780 --> 00:08.250
and Git Push, that we covered.

00:08.250 --> 00:09.900
All very important stuff.

00:09.900 --> 00:12.360
In this section, we are continuing to talk

00:12.360 --> 00:15.600
about working with remote repositories,

00:15.600 --> 00:17.490
specifically Git Hub repositories,

00:17.490 --> 00:20.700
but you could sub in Git Hub for other services.

00:20.700 --> 00:23.280
They're just not that popular, as we've already discussed.

00:23.280 --> 00:25.350
Specifically, we're focusing on two commands,

00:25.350 --> 00:27.450
Git Fetch and Git Pull.

00:27.450 --> 00:30.690
They both have to do with getting changes down

00:30.690 --> 00:33.840
from a remote repository, like a Git Hub Repo.

00:33.840 --> 00:35.460
So if we're working with collaborators

00:35.460 --> 00:37.347
and our repository changes,

00:37.347 --> 00:39.300
how do we get those changes down?

00:39.300 --> 00:42.570
We've seen the other half pushing up with Git Push.

00:42.570 --> 00:44.760
So there's only three topics, really,

00:44.760 --> 00:45.690
that are covered here.

00:45.690 --> 00:46.950
They're all connected.

00:46.950 --> 00:48.990
Something called Remote Tracking Branches,

00:48.990 --> 00:50.940
Git Fetch, and Git Pull.

00:50.940 --> 00:52.230
And I've marked them all in yellow

00:52.230 --> 00:55.140
because they are a bit, mm, I don't want to say trickier,

00:55.140 --> 00:59.370
but meatier, so they're all yellow.

00:59.370 --> 01:01.140
They're all critical.

01:01.140 --> 01:03.630
If you want to work with remote repositories,

01:03.630 --> 01:05.070
you could use Git your entire life,

01:05.070 --> 01:07.650
and never share your changes with anyone,

01:07.650 --> 01:08.940
at which point, you wouldn't need Git Hub.

01:08.940 --> 01:10.410
You wouldn't need to push, or to pull,

01:10.410 --> 01:12.090
or to fetch, or anything like that.

01:12.090 --> 01:15.161
But if you plan on collaborating, critical.

01:15.161 --> 01:15.994
All right?

01:15.994 --> 01:17.070
So let's talk about these commands,

01:17.070 --> 01:19.770
and get more practice working with Git Hub.

01:19.770 --> 01:20.603
Here we go.
